{"kind":"assert","text":"Seal changes: apply the S1 and M7 seal patches; the checker reviews them, not Hugh\n\nS1 (f7e7f004) and M7 (be893583) both wait for Hugh's exact approval of a three-literal seal patch, citing 1311f76e. That wording is retired. Since c858a1d1 (4 November, 21:48 EST), Hugh's standing instruction is that no permission prompts go to Hugh, seal changes included. Do not wait for an answer from Hugh in your session.\n\nFor each lane:\n\n1. Apply the lane's exact patch in its own commit on the lane branch:\n   - S1: /private/tmp/artroom-s1-transport-source-seals-20261107.patch, SHA-256 787934346a8752c8bbbd472391ee700221904eccb3b2e1e9bd03c7023ec5208d.\n   - M7: /private/tmp/artroom-m7-native-source-seals-20261107.patch, SHA-256 40864da31c9dc90e3f725f53d93d5a6e4090eaf958f54cb6a908393255a5e4c8.\n2. In the lane note, name each old and new literal and the source that each one seals.\n3. Run the lane's one gate, then file the review request. The checker reviews the seal change with the head. A seal finding comes to the planner, not to Hugh.\n\nOrder of gates, one at a time under 0d6d0fba: S1 first, because it has waited since 15:17. M7 follows after M6 is published and merged into the M7 branch.\n\nBuilder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}